From cbfaa749612a39241d0d1fb6552e23a465686b47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maxolgi <maxolgi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:46:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avformat: add websrt:// protocol (WebSRT via libwebsrt)

Publish (output) or subscribe (input) to a WebSRT gateway - SRT over
WebTransport - through libwebsrt's C ABI. Direction decides semantics:
an output publishes ?stream=NAME, an input subscribes to it, so the
same URL works verbatim on both sides.

URL: websrt://host:port?stream=NAME[&cert_hash=HEX][&cert_hash_file=PATH]
     [&pki=1][&latency_ms=N][&passphrase=...]
cert_hash_file parses the gateway's runtime cert-hash.js (CERT_HASH =
"<hex>" | null); with no cert parameter the protocol uses PKI.
passphrase is parsed and logged as reserved/ignored. MPEG-TS bytes are
framed by the library into 188-aligned SRT live messages of at most
1128 bytes; reads bounce through an internal one-message buffer;
writes loop over the library's partial-accept contract. Subscribing
retries HTTP 404 for up to 10 s (live-edge join), a stalled peer
bounds writes to 30 s and reads to 15 s.
---
